	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105027017148?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Department of Management, Islamic Azad University, Dubai, United Arab Emirates},
	abstract = {Developing energy-efficient super-smart cities transforms urban environments by integrating artificial intelligence of everything (AIoE), Internet of Thing, blockchain, and digital twins. These technologies enhance energy optimization, sustainability, and security but also introduce new cyber and physical threats. Ensuring a secure urban ecosystem requires artificial intelligence (AI)-driven predictive threat detection, blockchain-based identity management, and quantum-resistant encryption to mitigate emerging risks. AIoE-powered self-learning cybersecurity frameworks enable cities to autonomously detect, prevent, and respond to security threats in real time. Adopting decentralized authentication, zero-trust security models, and AI-enhanced biometric verification further strengthens urban resilience. Blockchain ensures data integrity and transparent energy transactions, while digital twins provide real-time security simulations to optimize infrastructure protection. As quantum computing advances smart cities must transition toward postquantum cryptography to safeguard sensitive communications. The future of smart city security depends on AIoE-driven automation, ethical AI governance, and harmonized cybersecurity regulations. By integrating autonomous cyber defense models, predictive security analytics, and decentralized risk mitigation strategies, cities can achieve a secure, efficient, and sustainable digital ecosystem capable of adapting to evolving threats and technological. Β© 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved..},
