	abstract = {In response to the critical vulnerabilities exposed by quantum computing and AI-driven cryptanalysis in traditional encryption systems, this article introduces NeuroCryptβ€”a neuro-symbolic AI framework that synergizes adaptive cryptography, decentralized governance, and postquantum security. NeuroCrypt employs three AI groups: CryptAI (multialgorithm encryption), GenAI (neuro-symbolic algorithm synthesis), and TestAI (adversarial validation), to dynamically generate and deploy quantum-resistant cryptographic techniques. The framework uniquely combines five-layer encryption (randomly ordered classical and AI-generated algorithms, e.g., latticeβ€“chaotic hybrids) with metadata-driven security, where encrypted logic is distributed via Shamirβ€™s secret sharing (SSS) over VPNs, eliminating key-exchange dependencies. A permissioned blockchain enforces tamper-proof updates validated by TestAI consensus (n/2 + 1 threshold), while dynamic threshold adaptation adjusts SSS shard requirements based on real-time threat levels. Evaluations demonstrate NeuroCryptβ€™s superiority: 2.3Γ— higher entropy than AES-256, 94.3% shard survival under 30% compromise, and 220 ms encryption latency for 1 MB data on edge devices. The systemβ€™s lattice-based encryption (1024-dimensional) and frequent AI-driven updates resist Shor/Grover attacks, validated through simulated quantum oracles achieving O(10<sup>38</sup>) operations for 256-bit keys. Compliance with GDPR, NIST PQC, and FIPS 140-2 ensures readiness for healthcare, fintech, and government applications. NeuroCryptβ€™s architectureβ€”backward-compatible with legacy systems and optimized for IoT/cloud ecosystemsβ€”sets a precedent for self-evolving security, offering a 15% storage overhead trade-off for metadata-driven keyless decryption. Future work will optimize edge-device performance and integrate 6G network protocols, establishing NeuroCrypt as a foundational framework for postquantum cybersecurity. Β© 2020 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {Adaptive encryption; artificial intelligence; blockchain; neural cryptography; neuro-symbolic AI; postquantum security; Shamirβ€™s secret sharing},
	keywords = {Blockchain; Data communication systems; Ecosystems; Encryption algorithms; Internet of things; Legacy systems; Metadata; Network architecture; Network protocols; Network security; Quantum cryptography; Adaptive encryption; Block-chain; CryptoGraphics; Metadata driven; Neural Cryptography; Neuro-symbolic AI; Post-quantum securities; Secret-sharing; Security and transmission; Shamirβ€™s secret sharing; Economic and social effects},
