	abstract = {The Internet of Things is currently transforming into massive heterogeneous networks that require ultra high speed and low-power wireless communication between a large number of sensors and actuators. Consequently, classic perimeter oriented security has become ineffective. To address this issue, this research paper proposes Quantum Resilient Zero Trust Edge AI Blockchain, a secure IoT system design that combines edge AI, federated and swarm intelligence, post quantum cryptography, and a permissioned blockchain that works alongside zero trust enforcement practice. Edge nodes enable sixth generation wireless and Wi Fi seven integrated with LoRaWAN and incorporate a zero-trust engine that applies a hybrid convolutional neural network classifier and transformer classifier at the edge for intrusion detection, and its model updating is synchronized via swarm learning based on proof of authentication blockchain ledger. Experiments on MU IoT dataset demonstrate accuracy of ninety-nine-point one percent, macro one of ninety-eight-point seven percent, sub millisecond inference latency, and average finality of one point three seconds on the ledger. Swarm learning is shown to enhance resilience against non iid and poisoning attacks for IoT networks, and post-quantum cryptography secures model updates and IoT identity transactions on this system. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
