	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105031578229?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Ege University, Graduate School of Natural and Applied Science, Izmir, Turkey},
	abstract = {Nowadays, drone technologies, also known as Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs), are utilized in numerous critical applications, including surveillance, rescue operations, and data collection. However, it is vulnerable to many attacks, including network security breaches, unauthorized access, and data theft. In addition, the threat posed by quantum computers' cryptographic methods makes network communication vulnerable. This study presents a new post-quantum secure blockchain-based network service architecture to provide effective network services in inter-drone communication. The proposed system is layer-based, and a hybrid encryption method integrated with ML-KEM is employed to counter quantum attacks. Additionally, it employs the dynamic Trust Weighted Proof of Authority (TW-PoA) mechanism, which is selected based on predefined trust parameters to determine the most suitable drone on the network. Finally, it provides a secure connection platform that offers low communication costs and overhead, utilizing blockchain and event-based smart contracts for secure data sharing. Experimental results show that the proposed system is applicable in terms of security, latency, and transaction efficiency.  Β© 2025 IEEE.},
